#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:1
msgid "Release 2.12 (2022-12-06)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:3
msgid ""
"On Linux, Nix can now run builds in a user namespace where they run as root "
"(UID 0) and have 65,536 UIDs available. This is primarily useful for running "
"containers such as `systemd-nspawn` inside a Nix build. For an example, see "
"[`tests/systemd-nspawn/nix`](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"blob/67bcb99700a0da1395fa063d7c6586740b304598/tests/systemd-nspawn.nix.)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:10
msgid "A build can enable this by setting the derivation attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:12
msgid ""
"```\n"
"requiredSystemFeatures = [ \"uid-range\" ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:16
msgid ""
"The `uid-range` [system feature](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-system-"
"features) requires the [`auto-allocate-uids`](../command-ref/conf-file."
"md#conf-auto-allocate-uids) setting to be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:21
msgid ""
"Nix can now automatically pick UIDs for builds, removing the need to create "
"`nixbld*` user accounts. See [`auto-allocate-uids`](../command-ref/conf-file."
"md#conf-auto-allocate-uids)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:26
msgid ""
"On Linux, Nix has experimental support for running builds inside a cgroup. "
"See [`use-cgroups`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-cgroups)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:30
msgid ""
"`<nix/fetchurl.nix>` now accepts an additional argument `impure` which "
"defaults to `false`.  If it is set to `true`, the `hash` and `sha256` "
"arguments will be ignored and the resulting derivation will have `__impure` "
"set to `true`, making it an impure derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:35
msgid ""
"If `builtins.readFile` is called on a file with context, then only the parts "
"of the context that appear in the content of the file are retained.  This "
"avoids a lot of spurious errors where strings end up having a context just "
"because they are read from a store path ([\\#7260](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/7260))."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:41
msgid ""
"`nix build --json` now prints some statistics about top-level derivations, "
"such as CPU statistics when cgroups are enabled."
msgstr ""
